{
  "_meta": {
    "capturedFrom": "pre-refactor single-file app (commit faa1ef9); mm_100x60x150_thin captured post-MIN_CALIPER-fix (raw caliper feeds compensation); in_8x6x5 re-baselined 2026-07-11 per engineering ruling: 15mm chamfer cap and raw caliper are the correct semantics, old inch-mode values (0.75in chamfer, 0.6in caliper floor) preserved in git history at commit 41d66bc",
    "note": "cut/crease/F/bbox are in the DISPLAY unit of each case (mm for cases 1-2 and the thin case, inches for case 3), exactly as the original geometry() produced them. Pallet: 48x40 in deck, 60 in max load height, all three stack patterns. flow-wrap chains re-baselined 2026-08-04 for END-SEAL ANGLES (feature/seal-angles): the end seal is no longer flush — internalAngle (film ramp, default 45) derives a jaw clearance per end and externalAngle (seal lay, default 45) sets how far the flexible fin stands; wrapOuter.L = productL + 2*(jawClearance + endSealWidth*sin(externalAngle)) at the CURRENT external lay (corrected 2026-08-04 from the earlier conservative-90deg-max sizing: the carton now FOLLOWS the actual seal lay, and packLengthMax is a reference only), growing every downstream carton/case/pallet metric. New pins wrap_seal_internal_steep (75deg) and wrap_seal_internal_mid (60deg) exercise the internalAngle->jawClearance cascade at the band. wrap_multi_per_carton_4x2 no longer palletizes at the default seals (case exceeds the GMA pallet) and now records 0 for the pallet metrics by design.",
    "date": "2026-08-04"
  },
